=====================================================================
1. GOAL
=====================================================================
A multi-agent competitive-intelligence pipeline. It monitors competitor product pages (changelog, blog, pricing). When a page changes, a chain of agents decides whether a real feature launched, how threatening it is to the user's product, and what the user should do. Every decision is written to a structured intelligence feed. The project also includes an evaluation harness that measures the system against a labeled dataset and runs ablations to prove the multi-agent design helps.

=====================================================================
2. HARD CONSTRAINTS
=====================================================================
- Python 3.11+. Windows-compatible: use pathlib, no Unix-only calls, no shell-specific commands in code.
- Free tier only. Primary LLM: Google Gemini via the google-genai SDK. Fallback LLM: Groq via the groq SDK. Both are optional at runtime. If a key is missing, skip that provider. If both are missing, raise a clear error.
- Scout, Diff-Engine, Evidence check, and Scribe are plain Python code, NOT LLM agents.
- Classifier, Analyst, and Strategist are LLM agents. Each loads its prompt from a text file in prompts/.
- All LLM calls go through ONE wrapper, src/llm.py.
- Temperature 0 for all LLM calls.
- Every agent output must be valid JSON matching a schema in src/schemas.py. Validate in code. On parse or validation failure, retry once with the error message appended to the prompt. If it fails again, mark the event status "parse_failed" and do not pass partial data forward.
- Nothing hardcoded: model names, thresholds, competitor URLs, product data, and paths all live in config.yaml.
- Secrets come from a .env file via python-dotenv. Never print or log API keys.

=====================================================================
3. AGENT WORKFLOW, ACCESS RULES, AND COMMUNICATION (ENFORCE IN CODE)
=====================================================================
Each agent sees only the fields listed in its "Reads" column. pipeline.py must build each agent's input from only those fields. This is what makes the information barriers real, not just documented.

| Agent | Type | Reads (access) | Must NOT see | Writes (output) | Sends to |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Scout | Code | Competitor URLs from config | Anything from other agents | Snapshot file per page per day | Diff-Engine |
| Diff-Engine | Code | Two snapshots: newest and previous for the same page | Product data, LLM output | DiffEvent (added text only), or None | Classifier |
| Classifier | LLM | Added text, competitor name | Product description, key features, roadmap, full snapshot | ClassifierOutput JSON | Pipeline: stops the event if not a launch |
| Analyst | LLM | Classifier output, competitor name, product description, key features, added text | Full snapshot, Strategist output | AnalystOutput JSON | Evidence check |
| Evidence check | Code | Analyst's evidence_quote, full snapshot text | Everything else | Pass, or status "invalid_evidence" | Strategist (only if pass) |
| Strategist | LLM | Analyst JSON output, product description | Raw snapshot, added text | StrategistOutput JSON (may contest Analyst) | Scribe |
| Scribe | Code | Full event record from all agents | Nothing is filtered | Appended feed entry, stdout digest | Feed file, Streamlit UI |

Communication rules:
1. Only the pipeline passes data between agents. Agents never call each other directly.
2. Each hand-off is a validated object. A failed agent stops that event with its failure status. Partial data is never forwarded.
3. Dropping is a decision and is logged. A dismissed event (Classifier says not a launch) is still written to the feed with status "dismissed", so evaluation can count false negatives. Diff-Engine drops (too small) are NOT logged to the feed, but are counted in the run summary.
4. Each agent's output and the model that produced it are recorded in the event record.

Event flow for one changed page:
Scout saves snapshot
 -> Diff-Engine: added text > min_diff_chars? No: count as "below_threshold", stop
 -> Classifier: is_feature_launch? No: log "dismissed", stop
 -> Analyst: threat + evidence_quote
 -> Evidence check: quote present verbatim in snapshot? No: log "invalid_evidence", stop
 -> Strategist: recommendation, may contest Analyst
 -> Scribe: append full record to feed, print digest line

